Yeah, it's been out for a few days. It's nice, but only incrementally 
better than Firebird, so don't worry about switching if it's a hassle.

Notably:

- (at least for Windows) installer .exe rather than just a .zip. Which 
may not be an advantage if you like the simplicity of the zipfile.

- The download manager is markedly different. sort of a "large icon" 
list view. Also, by default everything downloads to the desktop.

- find links/text as your type is controllable from the options window, 
as is automatic image resizing

- the add bookmark dialog is a little more powerful, though i still wish 
it would act like mainstream nethack and just add it to the root

- sundry bug fixes, of course

